{
  "milestone": "m1",
  "passed": false,
  "scope": "Desktop Chronicles on a production build: entry and loading, navigation by mouse, keyboard and a mocked standard controller, Back, the parity fixture replayed through the UI, motion and reduced motion, the flat fallback (WebGL disabled), layouts at 1280×720, 1920×1080 and 844×390, CDP measurements (long tasks with attribution, script time per frame, heap and canvases over round trips, the atmosphere rebuild, stage cost per preset) and one 4× CPU-throttled run.",
  "emulation": "Headless Chromium with SwiftShader software WebGL; controller input is a mocked standard Gamepad API device. Nothing here is GPU, desktop-hardware or headset evidence.",
  "checks": [
    "Home → Chronicles shows the loading state named by the approved title from the click, then the stage (ready in 4510 ms at medium on this host): a full-stage layer with the main navigation hidden and inert, the approved collection tabs only (no Contested Record) and one hidden button per nation",
    "Mouse: clicking each nation's marker on the stage opens exactly that nation's entry (title, body, label name and meaning) with its focus; Back closes the entry and keeps the nation, and Back again returns to the overview",
    "Clicks on bare ground, the painted map's centre included, change nothing",
    "Mouse: a drag orbits the view within its limits and the wheel zooms; neither opens an entry",
    "Pointer: moving onto a marker highlights and focuses its nation without changing the scene; a resting pointer never takes focus back from the keyboard",
    "Keyboard on the Atlas: arrows move the highlight spatially over the overview, browse to the neighbour's entry while one is open and carry the focus while a nation is focused; Enter opens, Escape unwinds, Home/End reach the ends, Shift+arrows orbit and plus/minus zoom, with a visible focus caption",
    "Collections switch by keyboard on the tabs (arrows, Home/End), by Q/E, by mocked LB/RB, by clicking the tabs and by clicking the LB/RB glyphs; Q/E and LB/RB cycle inside Chronicles and never reach the menu tabs",
    "The Interregnum and the Laws show every approved entry verbatim with its label over their framing; mouse and keyboard open them, arrows browse while one is open, Home/End reach the ends and Back closes the entry",
    "Behind the Interregnum and the Laws the relief settles, then rests receded on its last frame and issues no draw calls; no filter is applied to the stage",
    "Mocked standard controller: the D-pad and left stick move between nations and stops, A opens, B unwinds, the right stick orbits and the right trigger zooms the view, LB/RB cycle the collections",
    "Back (Escape, Backspace, B and the Back button) closes the entry, then the nation focus, then returns Home with the Chronicles tile selected and focused",
    "The shared parity fixture's 25 steps replay through the screen's own inputs (marker and ground clicks, arrows, Enter, Q/E, LB/RB, tab clicks, Escape, Backspace, B and the Back button) and every resulting state matches; the last Back returns Home",
    "Without WebGL the flat painting offers the same entries: four rings on their painted places (each at least 6% of the image width), the same records by pointer and keyboard, the Interregnum and the Laws, and Back returns Home",
    "A WebGL context lost after the stage is ready falls back to the flat painting with the same entries; the stage canvas is removed and Back still returns Home",
    "At 1920×1080, 1280×720 and 844×390 the Atlas, an open record, the Interregnum and the Laws fit without page overflow, clipped text, scrolling or overlapping panels, between the header and the footer, with Back reachable; hero frames at 1920×1080 (PNG)",
    "One render loop at a time with the real sorcerer: on Home the sorcerer drew 40 and the motes 40 calls in 40 frames; with Chronicles open only the stage drew and the menu's stage layers stopped compositing; on exit Home showed 12207 ms after Back, both menu loops resumed (first mote frame after 12258 ms) and the stage's canvas and context were released (12269 ms); exit long tasks, attributed: 11106.7 ms the stage's disposal (Chronicles); 59.6 ms garbage collection; 79.5 ms garbage collection",
    "After interactive at medium: 0 long task(s) over 50 ms in a 19134 ms traced window, none attributable to Chronicles (none); script per frame p50/p95/p99 1.44/4.13/4.13 ms",
    "Five Home ↔ Chronicles round trips: canvases back to 2 (stage 0); heap after GC 6.47 → 8.49 MB (2.02 MB; 0.7 MB since the first visit)",
    "Stage cost per preset (renderer.info) within budget at the overview and every nation framing: low overview 15 calls/57812 tris, heaviest overview 15/57812; medium overview 17 calls/226738 tris, heaviest overview 17/226738; high overview 17 calls/306474 tris, heaviest overview 17/306474",
    "Under 4× CPU throttling the screen appeared 94 ms after the click, the stage was ready after 14766 ms, and the collection switch took 154 ms; long tasks after interactive: [93]",
    "No JavaScript or console errors in any phase"
  ],
